god-files wholesale. **Product/design spec:** `rules/07-product-transfer.mdc`.

## Stack (do not "just this once") *(example — replace)*

- Async web framework on the prod runtime; fast JSON/dataclass serialization
  on the request path.
- Postgres, dedicated schemas per bounded context. Real FKs. Migration tool
  only — no boot DDL, no SQLite in prod.
- Cache/broker optional: the app runs degraded without it (no fan-out, empty
  presence, no perm cache) — it is an accelerator, never the source of truth.
- No heavy UI framework by default: native ESM + server templates; CSS
  variables (`--app-*`), no preprocessor.
- IDs: time-ordered UUIDs. Cookie = opaque session id. Object storage for media.
- One binary, role via env (`PROCESS_ROLE=api|worker|scheduler`).
- Staff URLs under a non-obvious prefix; the conventional `/admin` returns the
  same public 404 (no redirect).

## Where code goes *(example — replace)*

```text
app/<pkg>/               # import root — your package name
  identity / platform / social / app        # bounded contexts
    adapters/ → domain/ → infra/ + models/
  app/platform/core/     # master helpers — search here first
app/ui/lib/              # master JS helpers — look here first
app/ui_admin/            # staff-only frontend, served on its own asset path
```

Adapters have no business math. Domain has no framework types. Features do
not import other features.

## Authz (two planes) *(example — replace with your model)*

- **Staff plane** = categories + levels + per-person grants (internal
  dashboards, suspend, audit, break-glass).
- **Tenant plane** = per-member roles + channel/resource overlays (deny wins)
  + hierarchy.
- Elevated flags are re-derived server-side from the staff table — the raw
  actor flag is never trusted; adapters strip it.
- Gates (mute/raid/slow-mode) are gates, not permission keys.
- Privileged-view: reads only; writes 403; never elevates.
- Unknown catalog key = deny. UI snapshot is not enforcement.

## Performance reflexes *(keep or replace)*

- No blocking I/O on the request path. Timeouts on all egress.
- Tenant-scoped queries always filter the tenant key. Cursor pagination. No
  unbounded lists. No N+1.
- Events: transactional outbox, then fan-out. Private surfaces: entitlement
  fan-out, not broadcast.
- Heavy deps deferred; fetch permission snapshot before privileged chrome.

## UI reflexes *(keep or replace)*

- New UI = feature module + descriptor (routes, permissions, deferred load).
  No god-files.
- Chrome follows the design spec (`rules/07-product-transfer.mdc`): the design
  target decides the look. Where the spec is silent, keep the current chrome
  class. Never replace an overlay with a thin GET page or a "not wired yet"
  tile. Keep every feature — relocate rather than drop.
- One permissions helper (`canDo`-equivalent). `data-action="feature.verb"`
  per feature.
- Optimistic UI only where ordering is reconciled (e.g. chat with client ids).

## Security reflexes *(keep or replace)*

- CSRF + Origin on cookie mutations. WS auth from the session cookie — never
  tokens in query strings.
- Bound parameters. HTML allowlists. Magic-byte uploads. SSRF-safe egress. CSP
  nonces.
- Prod boot refuses: weak secrets, wrong DB, open CORS, DEBUG on, schema lag.

**Every slice:** maximum security, maximum performance, and modularity / code
quality are mandatory — not optional polish (`rules/05-sec-perf-modularity.mdc`).

## When implementing a slice

1. Open the matching task doc.
2. Read the plan section for that slice.
3. Search `docs/helpers-reference.md`; **widen** an almost-fit helper rather
   than a second copy.
4. One domain entrypoint per mutation.
5. Confirm IDOR (tenant id on load) + the permission you added, cite
   `file:line`. Tests optional.
6. Running the dev server is allowed (`rules/running-the-server.mdc`); don't
   needlessly disrupt a server another agent is using.
